what you are about to see is a review  written and recorded by my wife she has  never seen or read Hunter hunter before  and it is a completely blind impression  of episode 1 as a result she may  mispronounce you know a few names here  and there but hey that's fine now if you  like the sort of stuff please do let us  know with a like or comment down below  but for now enjoy the ramblings of my  wife hello and welcome to new world  review your source for everything  everything anime you are probably  expecting Liam's voice today you get me  his wife Chantal also known by me as  Grand Line waifu trying something new  I'm admittedly someone who doesn't watch  a great deal of anime or not as much as  I would like to be watching as someone  repeatedly hearing you need to watch  hunter hunter from their husband who  runs a channel discussing it no less I  thought it was probably time to say  goodbye for now to re watches of Kenshin  close the window with the last episode  of attack on titan say arigato and  farewell for now two food wars and  prepare myself for hunting squared bad  at maths and since there may be other  people out there who haven't seen it it  made sense at the time to share my  impressions of the first episode so if  you haven't seen it either or if you  have and are interested to hear how a  casual anime watcher sees the show this  first episode review may give you a bit  of an idea about what you're getting  yourself into and why there's so much  hype around a series that seems on the  surface to sit in the formula of a lot  of other series a literal Google search  tells me the series was directed by the  same director as my beloved rurouni  kenshin Kazuhiro for hoshi and that  among many other things explains why I  enjoyed watching the first episode of  the show episode 1 then it's very  focused on the idea of get out please  quick get out while maintaining the  appeal of the town to those who stay  it's it's gone immediately apart as a  bit of a curiosity and endearing  curiosity at that I do need to say that  the first half of the episode carried my  understanding of the second half if I  only half paid attention to the first  half I would have been entirely lost by  the second half and that's probably by  design the beginning serves to pick you  up and carry you on a journey the  writing is tight clear and very direct  in its storytelling and a joy to watch  everything I know about hunters the way  others think of them the way they hold  themselves the fact that gods father is  or was one and the  way he's discussed that's where I get my  information from the environment around  the main characters as well as those  characters discussing others  I value learning fact second hand if we  need to be told about someone and to go  back to the director I really appreciate  that he seems to insist that every  character big or small has a really  clear understanding of how they feel  toward a character they talk about it's  a credit to the entire team that they  give us that subliminal understanding  something I truly loved about Kenshin  was its commitment to complex emotions  the opening of Hunter hunter wasn't  complicated it resembled Pokemon and  seven deadly sins in so many ways that I  wondered whether I was going to be  watching another boy wanting to be the  very best and honestly I'm not as here  for that simplicity as I was when I was  seven however it very quickly left that  trope behind as I saw the relationship  Gaughan has with meto now I haven't  looked up anything beyond the creatives  involved in the anime to remain as  unbiased as possible and what stuck out  to me was the fact that as of episode 1  I actually don't know whom Ito is his  mum it seems odd that he calls her Mito  and that she uses his dad's name with  him a foster carer a friend her dad's  partner gone doesn't seem to be her  brother and he seems to take on wisdom  from her in a way that my sister  certainly didn't listen to my wisdom  when we were that age  despite watching and sort of analyzing  what I was seeing at first knowing I'd  be writing this review I felt myself  drawn to Mito in a way I hadn't expected  and I was glad she came up again whether  we see her again I have no idea but I  very much hope so because she set the  emotional tone for the episode in a way  that drew me in possibly more than any  other element the reasons for gone to  want to go and train to be a Pokemon  master I mean hunter and her reasons for  wanting him to stay were absolutely  evident in that opening half episode a  lot of information is very handily  communicated in that first 10 minutes  and as I reflect I feel I understand the  world a great deal more than I thought I  would after one episode but I'll come  back to that in fact of what are the  main cast for this first episode are  there reasons for leaving home seeking  to be hunters are intricately flawed as  someone with a deep interest in  psychology at drew me an annoyingly  quickly forgotten to be leaving to  understand his own abandonment makes me  wonder how long he's been trying to  catch that one fish yet the lightness  with which that opening scene is handled  makes me wonder whether gone is a  multi-faceted fool or trying to hide his  brokenness behind a smile  I also eagerly await the moment he gets  to meet his father and what kind of  reception he would get from that solemn  serious Cora pikas reason for leaving  home is simply vengeance in his case I'm  most interested to see whether he'll  compromise his desire for revenge when  he's face to face with those that killed  his people and by how much it's a very  clear set up and they didn't make us  wait to have that backstory information  though they teased that they might for  all of 90 seconds the game now is to see  whether that information comes into play  very quickly while it's still in our  minds or if we'll be left to forget it  and remember some information later I'm  sure there'll be a test lay or do dear  lay audio a comic relief lanky tall  older obsessed with respect and  recognition which he seems to think  he'll get with money by the end of the  episode we do sense there's hope for him  yet though the resolving exchange  between Korra pika and Li Oreo was  probably the whole lowest moment of the  episode for me it felt very much like we  needed to wrap things up because time  and so we wrapped it up I very much hope  the reason they were angry and why they  gave in so quickly after the storm is  something we can return to as the series  continues because while I understand  their motivations and why they were  angry I'm not certain I feel it's  justifiable to change your entire life  outlook after catching a boy flying out  to sea  then again I have never caught a boy  flying out to sea while I was in a jewel  situation I understand that it needed  resolving and having watched the  post-credits scene I can see that it's  not all hunky-dory but as someone who  may have stopped at the end of a single  episode I struggled being good people at  heart is a great concept but it's very  difficult to show in a shortened time  frame which I guess is exactly what  happened here  ah before I forget back to the world it  was entirely forgotten which is probably  why I forgot it - there was a lovely  picture of a seaside town a big fish  with crustacean legs the lord of the  lake told us that we weren't on earth  but somewhere similar somewhere with  hunter exams what is a hunter exam  no one knows especially not me all I  know is that it's worse than seasickness  a lot of things are worse than  seasickness maybe it's a clue to how  much sea travel there is in this world  can't be a hunter if you get seasick  after all really though despite being  reminded that the reason Gunn's leaving  home is to take the hunter exam to find  out why his dad just had to abandon him  the idea of the exam wasn't particularly  important to me  it got lost in the idea of travel and  became as important to the story in this  first episode anyway as the storm it was  an abstract way to get gone out of town  which is technically wrong because the  episode ended with the captain changing  his mind about them attempting the exam  which I'll admit wasn't hugely  believable for me either that kind of  really quick change was insane bordering  on absurd since the only one he really  spoke to was gone but let's brush that  under the rug of episode oneness we  can't fit everything in maybe that's why  it became less important to me as a plot  point ah music I haven't talked about  music and sound what an oversight from a  sometimes musician our first experience  of the show is a poppy poppy number  which combined with the cutesy features  of little GaN and friends my alternative  title for this show by the way  gone and friends all gone with friends  going through a preteen title sequence  of bright colors and cheesy grins gave  the impression of exactly the energy I  thought the hunter hunter episode would  have throughout in fact looking back at  it it's entirely possible that the  Pokemon vibe I got is heavily influenced  by the style of the music and the bright  colors involved in the opening title  I'll jump to the end title briefly  because I'm going to be heavily biased  and say I struggle with voice modulation  zin music it's a personal dislike of  mine and so I'm not actually going to  discuss the music in it other than to  say that the actual tone of the music  only somewhat fits the tone of the  episode we just saw with that in mind I  think it's important to highlight just  how much I love the practice of changing  theme music part way through anime  seasons what that will hopefully do in  this case and seems to have worked for  every other anime I've watched where  this happens is change the tone of the  series when things become fingers  crossed more serious further down the  line the music throughout the episode  seems very gone focused by that I mean  it's mostly up-tempo and playful which I  think adds to the youth of the episode  the composer seemed to be very much  pushing for the lightheartedness of the  environment what I find particularly  interesting though is that in moments of  depth the music fell away leaving the  focus on the voices more importantly  every scene with strong emotion depended  on the voice actor to carry it without  any sound effects to help bold design  choice if the actors went up to the task  luckily as I said they carried scenes  marvelously well so will I watch more  the answer is probably  I enjoy anime I enjoy the style of  animation unlike some I love held images  way to communicate heightened emotions  it's used a good effect here so I'm  hoping that continues and I'm hoping  these heightened emotional states and  the character focus conflicts that come  up continue to grow and develop  I think I'll continue to watch until I  feel I'm not getting that engagement or  until I'm just bored at a glance there  are 148 episodes to watch which is nice  I don't need to worry about running out  of episodes for around 3,000 minutes the  themes of the anime are already touching  on some of what I expect and hope to be  the core elements of the show family  friendship emotions tenacity and trust I  hope I continue to enjoy it and that is  all of my thoughts or most of my  thoughts the thoughts I could remember  on hunter hunter episode 1 if you  enjoyed this video and the content this  channel produces in general then please  do consider donating to the New World  review patreon because the support of  all of you amazing people is what  continues to make this channel possible  if patreon isn't quite your style then  please do leave this video a like share  or subscribe because it also helps  support this channel an incredible  amount and if you'd like to join the fun  then please do head over to the discord  server where a wide array of shenanigan  ori takes place on a daily basis and  finally please do comment with your  thoughts on departure and Friends  episode 1 of Hunter hunter this has been  the new world review and I'll see you  next time  [Music]

